# Railway's build only: the [leiden] extra on graphifyy (PRD-262 US-022), compiled
# with requirements.in into requirements-leiden.lock, which the Dockerfile's pybuild
# installs when INSTALL_GRAPH_EXTRAS=true (its default, Railway's build). The extra
# pulls graspologic, and with it POT, llvmlite, numba, statsmodels, gensim,
# scikit-learn and matplotlib, for one feature: Leiden clustering in the Knowledge
# Graph (graphify.cluster falls back to Louvain without it). The lock is compiled
# against requirements.lock, so every package the two share has the same version on
# Railway as in the published image and CI. PRD-262 US-027 deletes this file, its
# lock and the build arg.
graphifyy[leiden]==0.8.31
